      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2018-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Splitting the sum, \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\sum_{i=1}^{100}\\sum_{j=1}^{100}(i+j) \\\\ =\\sum_{i=1}^{100}\\sum_{j=1}^{100}i \\\\ {}+\\sum_{i=1}^{100}\\sum_{j=1}^{100}j \\\\ =100\\sum_{i=1}^{100}i \\\\ {}+100\\sum_{j=1}^{100}j. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nSince \\(\\sum_{k=1}^{100}k=5050,\\) this equals \\(100\\cdot5050\\) \\(+100\\cdot5050\\) \\(=1{,}010{,}000.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Split the sum into \\(\\sum\\sum i+\\sum\\sum j\\)",
        "The sum of the first \\(100\\) positive integers is \\(5050\\)"
      ],
